#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048459 :topic/id #uuid "a163637a-ed19-547a-85e8-0acfdb20fa0f" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087562 :question/id #uuid "07d823d0-39f8-5d70-8df4-7fd15783e148" :question/math-academy-id "e-5427" :question/problem "Are the following transformations linear?\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}_1:\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\t\n\\longrightarrow \n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2} \\\\ xy\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n\n\\mathbf{T}_2:\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\t\n\\longrightarrow \n\\begin{bmatrix}3x \\\\ x+2y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's consider $\\mathbf{T}_1.$ Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(kx)^{2} \\\\ (kx)(ky)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{k}^{2}{x}^{2} \\\\ {k}^{2}xy\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}k{x}^{2} \\\\ kxy\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne k{T}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textbf{T}_1$ is not a linear transformation.\n\nNow, let's consider $\\mathbf{T}_2.$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3kx \\\\ kx+2ky\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}k(3x) \\\\ k(x+2y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}3x \\\\ x+2y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\ ({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+2({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ ({x}_{1}+2{y}_{1})+({x}_{2}+2{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805617c9-a8c4-59a3-be62-a47fc477ffd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084705} {:answer/id #uuid "9be54c22-8f8d-5207-aca2-2613d0f04c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084706} {:answer/id #uuid "d97cecb1-de2a-5f51-a2d3-8b44939b8b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084707} {:answer/id #uuid "22ed53c4-84a1-50dd-8cc0-06dc752357a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084708} {:answer/id #uuid "428ff64d-dbe8-548e-9efe-2a1565e0d916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084709}] :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd9c0c9-ceec-5c81-8128-c630f394ddde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0f56867b-44b5-5e54-8a65-515646e8e908" :question/math-academy-id "q-12010" :question/problem "Let\n$$\n\\displaystyle T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x^{2} + y^{2} \\\\ 2x + 7y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $T(kv) = kT(v)$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n2. $T(v_{1} + v_{2}) = T(v_{1}) + T(v_{2})$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vectors $v_{1}$ and $v_{2}$\n3. $T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed20dcfb-93aa-5edf-8467-1766b4b4b822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477473} {:answer/id #uuid "d32af6f8-8b0f-5234-806c-62e9d747df5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d32af6f8-8b0f-5234-806c-62e9d747df5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c20384a-0816-5afd-a2d2-3cd169248491" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93078b9b-9d6c-5f09-8800-51a8a1ec8bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477475} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea56d0c-ed1c-5b1a-8bbd-91e911ada20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea56d0c-ed1c-5b1a-8bbd-91e911ada20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdecd740-b0ed-58be-95a9-c0e256d73db9" :answer-field/key "$T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4df3c9b-0f75-5bb2-b7f3-076984d785f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477477} {:answer/id #uuid "f15219cd-4112-5f94-bd53-1aa374fbf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f15219cd-4112-5f94-bd53-1aa374fbf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c819544-8a99-529a-8823-7309e6fe05a9" :answer-field/key "$T$ is a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477708} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f7adb9-b03b-5ccf-b4b6-058a03c8a4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668132} {:answer/id #uuid "cef7642b-6f96-5f33-9ceb-d096444d43c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6f7adb9-b03b-5ccf-b4b6-058a03c8a4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668132} :answer-field/id #uuid "65888345-1605-5140-8d16-6607988f0921" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9a96319-3bb3-5dd4-a3ac-27f5effab07d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8331" :question/problem "Let \n$$\n\\displaystyle T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}ky \\\\ kx\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253648 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "533214b3-6c61-52ee-85dd-a8d6006ced54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} {:answer/id #uuid "23c15b20-858c-5295-90c6-68f113ba9d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "533214b3-6c61-52ee-85dd-a8d6006ced54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} :answer-field/id #uuid "52121635-762f-5923-b01d-1582f7ea794d" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d6c812-7ee3-5e26-b033-2a4ef6caab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} {:answer/id #uuid "eba0a9bc-d740-58d4-9682-e24f2ebd01d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d6c812-7ee3-5e26-b033-2a4ef6caab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} :answer-field/id #uuid "b222fe66-ffd9-5e28-8684-edf53b486030" :answer-field/key "$T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462713} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1921f4a9-2a50-5748-bfbb-ee6ebd7a5229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461921} {:answer/id #uuid "2feb6598-cea3-599a-adb9-4e0e897d27ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2feb6598-cea3-599a-adb9-4e0e897d27ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922} :answer-field/id #uuid "79c1742e-b505-51ed-b84e-0e730cf0b35e" :answer-field/key "$T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462714} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b77aee-4838-5a9c-96f5-eeeb774fbd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667896} {:answer/id #uuid "28e306c7-56ef-5e46-8682-7096284c3742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b77aee-4838-5a9c-96f5-eeeb774fbd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667896} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad7d3c9-e10f-5b51-a15b-012aad4defbf" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a3a19c98-b506-54b2-aa6b-86aada819468" :question/math-academy-id "q-12012" :question/problem "Let \n$$\n\\displaystyle T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2} \\\\ 7y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(kx)^{2} \\\\ 7(ky)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{k}^{2}({x}^{2}) \\\\ k(7y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}k({x}^{2}) \\\\ 7y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2} \\\\ 7({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+7{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement “$T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfd51e38-d92a-5e3f-9610-a20858760152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465591} {:answer/id #uuid "31ed2499-deea-54d0-8415-eeb248c8c543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31ed2499-deea-54d0-8415-eeb248c8c543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465592} :answer-field/id #uuid "b686b9cb-12bd-5580-a6e3-c47ab3efa6d0" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id