c-8fa8-5763-af02-8040fb38cc1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-170589" :question/problem "If $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation and $\\,T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}=4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =T\\left(4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=4T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14429203-0bff-5bad-9ed4-c66dada52954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14429203-0bff-5bad-9ed4-c66dada52954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290718} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c1de91-fc34-5305-afc7-bcbc881452ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b0dd0d-12fa-50e1-b542-27981e