#uuid "71cd0047-bb0e-5e6f-8a23-200305fdb068" :question/math-academy-id "q-37870" :question/problem "If $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation and $\\,T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $\\,T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}=4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =T\\left(4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=4T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c348231-faac-5f15-ba88-4a5fcff9895b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393433} {:answer/id #uuid "1cbe61fb-3b9a-5b63-aefd-518ef08c77c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393434} {:answer/id #uuid "741f5285-7e52-5afa-8fd8-e7ffe7bb3ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393435} {:answer/id #uuid "3e486dbe-f3f0-57e0-8019-075933a8c6cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393436} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1aa637-1399-5be1-8754-cfd06e8753a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e1aa637-1399-5be1-8754-cfd06e8753a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393437} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d0c3af7-ad97-5864-bf2c-f087f946215b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "96c9c6b4-4b9d-5bd8-af24-21ff4fd8965e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74762" :question/problem "If $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation and $\\,T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}=4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =T\\left(4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=4T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\\right)=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087748 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087564 :question/id #uuid "e34b53de-72d8-541f-bd04-16d2cbf1e6b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5429" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}.$ If $\\mathbf{T}(4\\mathbf{v}_1+\\mathbf{v}_2)=\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_2)=\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},$ then find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{T}$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(4{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =4T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix} & =4T({v}_{1})+\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 4T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 4T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-32 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-32 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e373356c-ca65-508b-b3ce-86be086a7f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392155} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ccfa97-0ada-5f44-a085-95a786ab58df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392156} {:answer/id #uuid "bb05d848-1594-5666-99a3-fa1638c5fe2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392157} {:answer/id #uuid "12d10235-a42a-5dc8-946c-524f9738a777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392158} {:answer/id #uuid "c850e2f0-528a-5250-bfce-786943aff9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12d10235-a42a-5dc8-946c-524f9738a777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392158} :answer-field/id #uuid "312d0fd8-e696-5855-a9f3-81464b4b3a30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "43d33a73-244e-53cf-8482-6ff35fbd4bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-37871" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -19\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =2T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =2T({v}_{1})+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -19\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -19\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 22\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 22\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ea7471b-f07d-5136-abb7-edbd6a6c22d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392161} {:answer/id #uuid "bf986dff-1462-5e9f-94f9-b6d0d484764f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392162} {:answer/id #uuid "67342caa-f633-50fb-9dc2-4053e590cf91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392163} {:answer/id #uuid "89b4540a-daf5-5924-9891-f80197ce6f08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392164} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e112ba-48c8-504f-adb2-15695e08886d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf986dff-1462-5e9f-94f9-b6d0d484764f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392162} :answer-field/id #uuid "41610516-b0b1-5226-87ed-641ba05d065c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "00d97500-f2d6-5911-b246-c9aee29ac1dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-37898" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235515 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "803f1f1c-7d91-56fa-88d8-a91d1c2cd014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "803f1f1c-7d91-56fa-88d8-a91d1c2cd014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234741} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c5b811a-cc8d-5181-924f-f714dc90973f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862103c6-c9bd-5184-8e41-07946fc9317a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862103c6-c9bd-5184-8e41-07946fc9317a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234748} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ff1cc15-8098-5d88-80fb-b53b1392a3e5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8daadc4-e7fb-582e-84dd-e6c2d25221e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8daadc4-e7fb-582e-84dd-e6c2d25221e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234914} :answer-field/id #uuid "c99e9f94-0f7b-57f8-8f45-a8c6336d0274" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "78adb41e-3609-50ab-8c29-8ae393119cc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-168037" :question/problem "The helicopter's pilot wants to consider the effect of a linear transformation $T$ such that $T(r)=⟨-8,17,3⟩$ and $T(3q+r)=⟨10,17,9⟩.$ Find the image of $q$ under the action of $T.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$T(q)=\\,⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kq+hr)=T(kq)+T(hr)=kT(q)+hT(r)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $q$ and $r.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3q+r) & =3T(q)+T(r) \\\\ ⟨10,17,9⟩ & =3T(q)+⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨10,17,9⟩-⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =⟨6,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82fa39fa-d638-5008-9c08-aedaac44bbdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82fa39fa-d638-5008-9c08-aedaac44bbdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291185} :answer-field/id #uuid "1298dca7-b6db-538d-a8ef-8a30820933cf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f06c7cc2-4ba0-5e87-8d7f-5ffc8d1dc4dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f06c7cc2-4ba0-5e87-8d7f-5ffc8d1dc4dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291638} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b54103b-15cc-531b-838b-e2908d82651d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd93b7d3-860a-5153-a2e2-a1c54e1634a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-275670" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+2{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $T({v}_{2}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{2})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+2{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+2T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+2T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 2T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 2T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299641 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a02dc7fd-a55a-5c76-b2cd-2feb4cba877b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a02dc7fd-a55a-5c76-b2cd-2feb4cba877b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298258} :answer-field/id #uuid "0467062b-d649-538f-9c77-dc029fd88d04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298652} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bee585cb-de79-565c-947a-33064f58606c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bee585cb-de79-565c-947a-33064f58606c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298389} :answer-field/id #uuid "1038e7bd-a456-58ed-bdb4-3a175b27b2a8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ccff3f5-2317-563c-af12-25f8ff047ae3" :question/math-academy-id "q-317716" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(-5{v}_{1}+4{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}23 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-kv+hw)=T(-kv)+T(hw)=-kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-5{v}_{1}+4{v}_{2}) & =-5T({v}_{1})+4T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}23 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix} & =-5T({v}_{1})+4\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}23 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}23 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-35 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-35 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7b2496b-dba2-56f2-af9f-53b63908d0fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7b2496b-dba2-56f2-af9f-53b63908d0fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298349} :answer-field/id #uuid "c47f53f4-5e38-584b-a524-b3d84c109986" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61c388b8-ce86-5c04-b99b-8037f66461f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61c388b8-ce86-5c04-b99b-8037f66461f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297968} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2bf8dd0-e792-552d-9de9-0396cbb49a56" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ee352f1-381d-59d6-bf49-efc95302ce91" :question/math-academy-id "q-317722" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(-6{v}_{1}+5{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -39\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-kv+hw)=T(-kv)+T(hw)=-kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-6{v}_{1}+5{v}_{2}) & =-6T({v}_{1})+5T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -39\\end{bmatrix} & =-6T({v}_{1})+5\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =5\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -39\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -39\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299643 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7b507ea-38a1-53c4-90df-73b715056379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7b507ea-38a1-53c4-90df-73b715056379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298607} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7b16a57-503f-5b9b-a3bc-7d6273799178" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5b1e75b-9b2e-5222-bb62-397b3eacd2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5b1e75b-9b2e-5222-bb62-397b3eacd2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298538} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80fc6e0-3afa-5bed-9064-d4bf837a75ae" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e63e02fd-0471-5470-a3c7-b8b9aafe03db" :question/math-academy-id "q-317745" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} & =3T({v}_{1})+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299644 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc78a065-a295-5326-96f6-dcd41a4da404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc78a065-a295-5326-96f6-dcd41a4da404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298497} :answer-field/id #uuid "993882dd-9e5d-5a46-938b-6dab19e4bace" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c8c348-ad59-5343-9782-d47363a1ff45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01c8c348-ad59-5343-9782-d47363a1ff45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297563} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4bde083-7383-5be7-aad2-85a81ac89efb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "af8ba7d5-d8e9-5ab4-b0e6-71cb8c5a26b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-317817" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix} & =3T({v}_{1})+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dbb1f6f-0919-5e14-aab3-63dd031f318d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342622} {:answer/id #uuid "4deb3204-83bd-5f97-bdb5-4b404d233cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342877} {:answer/id #uuid "5fefe333-55f2-55d9-bd5f-c129617c8ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343053} {:answer/id #uuid "acc17cbd-959f-5889-ae39-3ece2c5151f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343759} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0bf072-44c5-5d87-8181-aa62fe42d3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd0bf072-44c5-5d87-8181-aa62fe42d3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343900} :answer-field/id #uuid "7318bc52-e9d3-5153-a2f5-88eca1ef6902" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2c55eb86-992c-5929-994c-e27a136f03fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-74769" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(-2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =-2T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} & =-2T({v}_{1})+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ -2T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ -2T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "583bad78-a483-5e27-bf47-58fa7202f27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342976} {:answer/id #uuid "6be637e4-9438-50fa-8eae-7474192f1762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343157} {:answer/id #uuid "9370f90d-c9b1-5bfd-8975-b97002f0395d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343529} {:answer/id #uuid "a785af97-7aca-578f-a428-4801508b0088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343712} {:answer/id #uuid "d623a847-954d-5cb4-8a03-08d4a77a89db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "583bad78-a483-5e27-bf47-58fa7202f27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342976} :answer-field/id #uuid "09ef93ff-b1a6-5f21-8b6f-950d9d095354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "74809f1e-86dc-5e20-b04f-3f1424b7f6d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74771" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+5{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+5{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+5T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+5T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 5T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 5T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49cf9e39-72e2-58f9-b054-455b37ef9011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342846} {:answer/id #uuid "631c5cf6-23fc-5295-927c-c35fd65028d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343075} {:answer/id #uuid "6540d294-e2a1-52db-89de-e2012cde3668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343096} {:answer/id #uuid "8bde63a2-2e95-54b6-b901-af12256288f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343460} {:answer/id #uuid "c9074965-facc-5be3-a5a7-b0339e9ae4cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bde63a2-2e95-54b6-b901-af12256288f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343460} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc3bc1af-3c50-5249-9908-4663f13315fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c539f085-7e27-5313-a8d5-447fe9bd7096" :question/math-academy-id "q-74773" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(2{v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+hw)=T(kv)+T(hw)=kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2{v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =2T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =2T({v}_{1})+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e37951b-03d5-5d76-8207-ab35ada60274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342489} {:answer/id #uuid "6884287b-be82-539e-a37e-d742e488e1f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343130} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd306d4-ea1c-535c-800d-cf76b50ffc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343199} {:answer/id #uuid "bd29d454-d450-573b-992f-b35c8afcb1e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343901} {:answer/id #uuid "e53aba8b-8d6b-5204-b078-e2ccc56fd5f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e37951b-03d5-5d76-8207-ab35ada60274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342489} :answer-field/id #uuid "761eb299-8f17-5fa6-8798-80c42abd8f3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c7ac2355-a1ae-54c5-9e5b-62d94023dff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74775" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(3{v}_{1}+7{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+hw)=T(kv)+T(hw)=kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+7{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+7T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =3T({v}_{1})+7\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393438 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44d858c6-36e5-5228-a036-e8c30e129ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393440} {:answer/id #uuid "b18343b0-1c7e-5b30-98ce-ceafad393a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393441} {:answer/id #uuid "b84042c5-ba1a-5cd7-9cc2-1b2349158b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393442} {:answer/id #uuid "51d9493e-7fde-5dc6-bef8-ba7a9dbe9b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393443} {:answer/id #uuid "34eb6041-c57a-5542-a98e-005314b126f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b18343b0-1c7e-5b30-98ce-ceafad393a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393441} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7bae7b3-cdd8-57c9-ab74-b804a04463ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d3aabb18-a945-51e2-bce9-9f0029a0d83e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74774" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(4{v}_{1}-5{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+hw)=T(kv)+T(hw)=kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(4{v}_{1}-5{v}_{2}) & =4T({v}_{1})-5T({v}_{2}) \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-5T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 5T({v}_{2}) & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 5T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 5T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186603024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75059809-6ae6-5142-a2db-f78b089dc312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75059809-6ae6-5142-a2db-f78b089dc312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602697} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c6108ca-2180-5a2b-8ffa-186e99034922" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5128d0e-6427-5eb0-a652-e1582520da6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5128d0e-6427-5eb0-a652-e1582520da6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602796} :answer-field/id #uuid "743c7c24-6577-5500-bf3e-cc8e17ebcba8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602925} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1eabd6f-9266-501b-9a8c-de4e34afbe08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1eabd6f-9266-501b-9a8c-de4e34afbe08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602842} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9007ad-37ee-587e-9dc8-cfcbe8b99346" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3209e177-5bd7-57ff-b50b-07eab5198553" :question/math-academy-id "q-168044" :question/problem "Susan wants to consider the effect of a linear transformation $T$ such that $T(c)=⟨-3,-3,9⟩$ and $T(c-2b)=⟨-5,3,-7⟩.$ Find the image of $b$ under the action of $T.$\n\n$T(b)=\\,⟨$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kb+hc) &=T(kb)+T(hc)=kT(b)+hT(c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $b$ and $c.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(c-2b) & =T(c)-2T(b) \\\\ ⟨-5,3,-7⟩ & =⟨-3,-3,9⟩-2T(b) \\\\ 2T(b) & =⟨-3,-3,9⟩-⟨-5,3,-7⟩ \\\\ 2T(b) & =⟨2,-6,16⟩ \\\\ T(b) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨2,-6,16⟩ \\\\ T(b) & =⟨1,-3,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7a9a91f-30fc-51f0-bfbc-08ec16e9f857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7a9a91f-30fc-51f0-bfbc-08ec16e9f857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604435} :answer-field/id #uuid "2464e804-1024-523a-8167-d134ad41ffea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604483} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bcdf5ed-3886-5178-ae3c-a9461f322ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bcdf5ed-3886-5178-ae3c-a9461f322ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604326} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b48dcfc-13e7-5570-8a1a-3bf49ac91461" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d17707-e10f-538c-9c36-cba2b2ac994e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32d17707-e10f-538c-9c36-cba2b2ac994e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604263} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae0dced8-7b14-5487-93af-70b56e732530" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "88a5b6a3-7566-5260-90ed-8a3fa73155f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-168030" :question/problem "Tom wants to consider the effect of a linear transformation $T$ such that $T(w)=⟨6,0,-4⟩$ and $T(u-2w)=⟨-2,6,8⟩.$ Find the image of $u$ under the action of $T.$\n\n$T(u)=\\,⟨$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(ku+hw) &=T(ku)+T(hw)=kT(u)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $u$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(u-2w) & =T(u)-2T(w) \\\\ ⟨-2,6,8⟩ & =T(u)-2⟨6,0,-4⟩ \\\\ ⟨-2,6,8⟩ & =T(u)-⟨12,0,-8⟩ \\\\ T(u) & =⟨-2,6,8⟩+⟨12,0,-8⟩ \\\\ T(u) & =⟨10,6,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087749 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087565 :question/id #uuid "fc3159fb-751c-55d6-b41e-4744b80b0ae9" :question/math-academy-id "e-5430" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}.$ If $\\mathbf{v}_1 + \\mathbf{v}_2=\\mathbf{0}$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1)=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},$ then find $\\mathbf{T}(17\\mathbf{v}_1+12\\mathbf{v}_2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $\\mathbf{v}_1 + \\mathbf{v}_2=\\mathbf{0},$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2} & =5{v}_{1}+12{v}_{1}+12{v}_{2} \\\\  & =5{v}_{1}+12({v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =5{v}_{1}+12(0) \\\\  & =5{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}(17\\mathbf{v}_1+12\\mathbf{v}_2)=\\mathbf{T}(5\\mathbf{v}_1).\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\mathbf{T}$ is a linear transformation, we have that $\\mathbf{T}(k\\mathbf{v})=k\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(5{v}_{1}) & =5T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =5\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ -60 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $\\mathbf{T}(17\\mathbf{v}_1+12\\mathbf{v}_2)=\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ -60 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fbd335c-28cc-5f02-b773-f685e8b15417" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05950c08-5c08-5eef-8c96-39dd0a499930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321195} {:answer/id #uuid "24517cd9-3cd2-5e3f-aa2a-acbf769d4c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321428} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9db913-7baf-5b2f-890d-999fcca06626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}108 \\\\ -72 \\\\ 60\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321597} {:answer/id #uuid "bf938989-2e7b-556c-8e39-45affa13e016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322634} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4f0a97-6e05-5d11-82ae-a97239669a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}27 \\\\ -18 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf938989-2e7b-556c-8e39-45affa13e016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322634} :answer-field/id #uuid "58d2bcaa-18ae-5115-a991-758d3115c797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "edb52688-79ea-5f71-b873-96bf082190d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-37873" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=\\begin{bmatrix}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}\\,$, find $\\,T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} & =18{v}_{1}+3{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} \\\\  & =18({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =18(0)+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =3{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=T(3{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}) & =3T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =3\\begin{bmatrix}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d67dd171-760d-5486-b3f7-56d80c2756a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-48 \\\\ 36 \\\\ 60\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085555} {:answer/id #uuid "149272c4-bd63-5210-ba74-47dc48d4144f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-36 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 45\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085556} {:answer/id #uuid "1f2d3e4c-12bb-56a0-9fa9-83424bcddd36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-24 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085557} {:answer/id #uuid "44f80e9b-8bb0-52fd-a953-ffb664af5bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085558} {:answer/id #uuid "722337cf-5064-5645-9454-4697ac2f0ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-60 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 75\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085559}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f6eeeeb4-f7d7-5194-9861-ba775d74d6ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085554}] :question/id #uuid "590c099f-8ba7-5c6d-8543-41afb4123917" :question/math-academy-id "q-37902" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$. If $v_{1} + v_{2} = 0$ and $T(v_{2}) = \\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}$, find $T(15v_{1} + 19v_{2})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284659 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19625734-7113-5821-bfe0-4875b25d5510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-55 \\\\ 36 \\\\ 60\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281920} {:answer/id #uuid "4f1a69eb-b918-539b-be59-b72fcf2862c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282368} {:answer/id #uuid "855eca06-a3d8-59c2-921c-972344e3256e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-60 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282840} {:answer/id #uuid "900cd049-8c48-57d7-bf4c-46f5aa46a068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-75 \\\\ 48 \\\\ 60\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282937} {:answer/id #uuid "f774ee27-a42c-5f92-be5e-44a7d06dbd30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-60 \\\\ 36 \\\\ 54\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "900cd049-8c48-57d7-bf4c-46f